--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,13 @@
 # Drift / Atlas workspace — main version
 
+## Accuracy update
+
+New curve searches use accuracy protocol 1: four fresh matched pairs (eight trials), packet-arrival diagnostics, frame-time percentiles and task-level guards. A result stays provisional until the same candidate repeats on two distinct days with matching mouse identity and practical tracking/comfort clearance. Earlier searches retain their original protocol and measurements.
+
+Open **Converters > Measure physical sensitivity** for three ruler-based swipes and an optional independent in-game turn-distance check. Configured DPI and measured effective CPI remain separate. The tool saves a local report; it never changes a mouse or driver setting. Neutral input and ruler distances are user confirmed.
+
+Run `test.ps1` for isolated regression, accuracy and calibration-layout checks. Run `accuracy-check.ps1` for the additional read-only comparison against the installed official Raw Accel 1.6.1 calculator. Calculator agreement does not verify hardware timing or physical sensor accuracy. Public implementation notes and the portable source patch are in the parent project's `docs/DRIFT_ACCURACY.md` and `source-import/drift/accuracy-pass.patch`.
+
 This folder is the primary Drift project from October 30, 2026. Open `SensitivityFinder.exe` here. The former D: project is a backup, not the active source.
 
 Version 6.1.1 adds Atlas midnight/blue styling, compact workspace views, grouped metadata labels, profile collection tabs and an updated Guide. It preserves the native calibration, evidence and deliberate driver workflows. The previous executable and changed UI sources are backed up under `backups/atlas-ui-pass-1/`.
